INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Living Jedi Testament IV: Discipline','jedi-testament-discipline','Discipline is the practice of choosing conduct deliberately, even when emotions are intense. It is not the absence of emotion. Fear may identify danger, anger may reveal injustice, and grief may express attachment to something valuable. None automatically determines the appropriate response.

Develop discipline through achievable commitments, reflection and correction. When a commitment fails, examine the circumstances rather than imposing punishment. Rest and assistance can sustain responsibility.

Practice: identify a recurring difficult situation, write down your usual response and choose a constructive alternative. Review the outcome without demanding perfection.

Question: when does restraint become avoidance, and when does action become impulsiveness?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Living Jedi Testament V: Service','jedi-testament-service','Service is the voluntary application of one''s abilities to the welfare of others. It does not require self-erasure, unquestioning obedience or neglect of one''s own needs. A guardian listens before intervening and evaluates whether assistance actually helps.

Service may take the form of teaching, repairing, caring, creating or defending another person''s dignity through lawful means. The value of an act is not determined by its visibility or the prestige it earns.

Practice: select a manageable community need, obtain consent where appropriate, contribute a useful skill and ask for feedback. Record what worked and what should change.

Question: how can a community distinguish genuine service from the pursuit of recognition?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Living Jedi Testament VI: Impermanence','jedi-testament-impermanence','All relationships, institutions and circumstances change. Recognizing impermanence does not require denying love or avoiding commitment. It means acknowledging that care cannot guarantee possession or permanence.

Grief is a meaningful response to loss. A spiritual path should allow mourning, remembrance and support rather than demanding immediate serenity. Acceptance concerns recognizing reality; it does not require approving every event.

Practice: reflect on a change in your life, identify what remains meaningful and choose a constructive way to honor it. Private reflection is sufficient.

Question: how can devotion coexist with the recognition that another person''s future is not ours to control?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Living Jedi Testament VII: Accountability','jedi-testament-accountability','Accountability connects ethical intentions to actual consequences. A guardian who causes harm must be willing to listen, acknowledge responsibility and pursue reasonable repair. Good intentions alone do not erase an outcome.

Institutions also require accountability. Teachers and leaders should be subject to transparent standards, independent review and the same rules as students. Spiritual status is never immunity from criticism.

Practice: examine a mistake, distinguish your responsibility from circumstances outside your control, and identify a specific corrective action. Respect another person''s choice not to reconcile.

Question: what safeguards prevent a community devoted to virtue from becoming convinced of its own infallibility?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The Sovereign Flame IV: Victory','sith-flame-victory','Victory is the achievement of a deliberately chosen objective. It need not involve an enemy. Completing a difficult project, breaking an unhelpful habit or gaining independence may represent a more enduring triumph than defeating a rival.

Examine the price of success. An achievement that destroys the capabilities, relationships or values necessary for future freedom may be a strategic failure. Changing an objective in response to evidence is not surrender.

Practice: define success before beginning a project, including measurable outcomes, acceptable costs and conditions for revision. Review results honestly.

Question: if an achievement requires permanent dependence on a rival, in what sense has the victor become free?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The Sovereign Flame V: Liberation','sith-flame-liberation','Liberation concerns the expansion of meaningful choice. External constraints, inherited expectations and internal habits can all restrict agency. Recognizing a constraint is the beginning of examining it, not proof that it can immediately be removed.

Interdependence is not necessarily captivity. Voluntary commitments and mutually beneficial relationships can enlarge freedom. The distinction lies in consent, alternatives and the ability to renegotiate boundaries.

Practice: identify one limiting dependency, determine which parts are changeable and plan a realistic step toward greater independence. Avoid abrupt decisions that jeopardize essential needs.

Question: can freedom include obligations freely chosen and consistently honored?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The Sovereign Flame VI: Shadow','sith-flame-shadow','Shadow is used here as a metaphor for aspects of experience that a person avoids acknowledging. It may include envy, fear, shame, ambition or even strengths that conflict with an established self-image. Acknowledgment does not require acting on every impulse.

Examine contradictions with curiosity and evidence. Distinguish what you feel from what you intend and what you actually do. Reflection is not a substitute for professional care when distress becomes overwhelming.

Practice: choose a manageable recurring reaction, identify its context and possible purpose, and develop an alternative response consistent with your chosen values. Keep sensitive reflections private.

Question: when does identifying with a dark self-image become another form of confinement?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The Sovereign Flame VII: Responsibility','sith-flame-responsibility','Sovereignty requires ownership of decisions and their consequences. Claiming credit for success while assigning every failure to others undermines self-knowledge. Responsibility means accurately distinguishing personal choices, shared obligations and circumstances outside one''s control.

A sovereign may revise a commitment, admit an error or repair harm without surrendering independence. Leadership requires transparent agreements and accountability rather than demands for unconditional loyalty.

Practice: review a consequential decision, identify foreseeable effects and compare them with the outcome. Determine what you would repeat, revise or repair.

Question: how can a philosophy of personal power remain coherent if its adherents refuse responsibility for how that power affects others?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';